    "narrative": "The highlight of today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP is **Brice Turang**, who commands a Strong 65.44 efficiency score. Even with his lineup spot currently pending, he is an auto-start; our projection models favor his matchup against Roki Sasaki, specifically leveraging the pitcher's slow delivery to the plate, which significantly inflates **Brice Turang**'s stolen base potential\u2014the most critical asset for our roster construction. Joining him in the productive tier is **Travis Bazzana** (56.66), whose favorable platoon edge against the 4.43 xERA of Montero provides a solid floor for batting average and run production, effectively buffering against the tougher arms elsewhere in the lineup.\n\nOur strategy today forces some difficult benching decisions, primarily due to the team\u2019s current injury landscape. While **Josh Naylor** (54.98) and **Seiya Suzuki** (52.65) make the cut, both face high-tier arms in Fried and Cavalli, respectively, leading to tempered expectations despite their roles near the top of their respective orders. **Jose Caballero** remains our most marginal start at 44.61; while he lacks an elite projection against Gilbert, he remains active solely to chase his unique speed profile in a tight 5x5 race. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood** and **Trevor Story**, whose absence from the active roster remains the primary constraint on our daily ceiling, forcing us to rely on utility depth like **Zach McKinstry**, **Max Muncy**, and **Isaac Paredes** to fill gaps as needed. With **Corbin Carroll** and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined by schedule gaps, we are currently prioritizing situational speed and platoon-favorable matchups over raw power, betting that the stolen base volume from **Brice Turang** and the order-placement boosts for **Seiya Suzuki** will carry the offense through these challenging individual matchups.",
